<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>StAX-XML Wasm Smoke</title>
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      background: #f5f7fb;
      color: #172033;
    }

    main {
      max-width: 880px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 24px;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 32px;
      line-height: 1.15;
    }

    p {
      color: #4f5b6f;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .status {
      margin: 28px 0;
      padding: 16px 18px;
      border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: white;
      font-weight: 650;
    }

    .status[data-status="ok"] {
      border-color: #16a34a;
      color: #166534;
      background: #f0fdf4;
    }

    .status[data-status="error"] {
      border-color: #dc2626;
      color: #991b1b;
      background: #fef2f2;
    }

    pre {
      overflow: auto;
      min-height: 180px;
      padding: 18px;
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: #111827;
      color: #e5e7eb;
      font: 13px/1.5 "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, monospace;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <h1>stax-xml Wasm Package Smoke</h1>
    <p>
      This page imports the browser export of @stax-xml/native-wasm32-wasi through
      the Astro/Vite dev server and executes a small parse. The browser console
      logs the final evidence under [stax-xml wasm smoke].
    </p>
    <div id="wasm-status" class="status" data-status="pending">Waiting for wasm smoke...</div>
    <pre id="wasm-output">{}</pre>
  </main>

  <script>
    import "../../scripts/wasm-smoke.ts";
  </script>
</body>
</html>
